# SharpTS Homebrew tap

Apple Silicon macOS casks for the SharpTS TypeScript interpreter and compiler. Choose one:

```sh
# Default: full-feature self-contained managed CLI
brew install --cask nickna/tap/sharpts

# Alternative: Native AOT CLI with the limitations below
brew install --cask nickna/tap/sharpts-native
```

Both casks install `sharpts`, include their CLI runtime and conflict with each other. Intel Macs
are unsupported. A separate .NET installation is not needed to run the CLI; executing generated
managed DLL output requires a compatible .NET host.

```sh
sharpts --version
```

The managed SKU provides the full CLI feature set. The Native AOT SKU uses a closed .NET interop
catalog: arbitrary DLL/NuGet references, `--verify`, `--gen-decl` and compiled `child_process.fork`
require the managed SKU. See the upstream [Native AOT contract](https://github.com/nickna/SharpTS/blob/main/docs/native-aot.md).

Upgrade or uninstall the cask you installed:

```sh
brew upgrade --cask nickna/tap/sharpts
brew uninstall --cask nickna/tap/sharpts

# Equivalent operations for the alternative SKU
brew upgrade --cask nickna/tap/sharpts-native
brew uninstall --cask nickna/tap/sharpts-native
```

Switch from managed to Native AOT:

```sh
brew uninstall --cask nickna/tap/sharpts
brew install --cask nickna/tap/sharpts-native
```

Switch back:

```sh
brew uninstall --cask nickna/tap/sharpts-native
brew install --cask nickna/tap/sharpts
```

Casks use immutable stable-release URLs and hashes. Both released Apple Silicon executables must
pass Developer ID signature, notarization and online Gatekeeper checks. No Gatekeeper bypass is
part of installation; a bare CLI executable does not provide a stapled offline-install ticket.
Report CLI defects to [SharpTS](https://github.com/nickna/SharpTS/issues) and cask installation
problems to this tap. Release and update procedures are maintained in the upstream
[distribution guide](https://github.com/nickna/SharpTS/blob/main/docs/homebrew-distribution.md).
